## 1. Agreement

By installing, building, accessing or using Kanaru (the "Software"), including
its source code, you agree to this Agreement. If you do not agree, do not use
the Software.

## 2. Definitions

- **Personal, non-commercial use** means using the Software yourself, on your
  own devices, to listen to and manage your music, including at work or while
  doing paid work that is not about the Software. It does **not** include
  selling, renting or licensing the Software; offering it, or a service built
  on it, to others; bundling it with a product or device; or using it, or its
  code, to earn money or another commercial advantage.
- **Official build** means a build of the Software published by the owner,
  unmodified.
- **Written permission** means permission from the owner sent from the contact
  address above.

## 3. What you may do

Kanaru is **source available**. Subject to this Agreement, you get a personal,
non-exclusive, non-transferable license, without a fee, to:

- install and use the Software for personal, non-commercial use;
- read the source code, build it and modify it for personal, non-commercial use
  or personal learning;
- modify the source code to contribute changes back to Kanaru (section 12).

## 4. What you may not do

Unless you have written permission, you may not:

- use the Software, its source code or any part of them beyond section 3, in
  particular for a commercial purpose or in another product;
- redistribute, sublicense, sell, rent or lease the Software, modified or not,
  except as section 5 allows;
- remove or change this Agreement, copyright notices or attributions.

## 5. Approved distribution of official builds

Official builds may be redistributed free of charge, with the name, branding
and this Agreement intact, through:

- Google Play;
- GitHub Releases of the Kanaru repository;
- Flathub;
- the Arch User Repository (AUR) and Nix / nixpkgs, as packages that install an
  official build or build the published source without changes other than
  those needed to package it;
- the Apple App Store, once an iOS version exists.

The owner may add places to this list in later versions of this Agreement or by
written permission.

## 6. Name and logo

"Kanaru" and the Kanaru logo identify the official Software. A modified version
or fork may not use the name or the logo, or suggest that it is the official
Software, without written permission.

## 7. Ownership

The Software and all intellectual property rights in it belong to the owner.
This Agreement grants a license; it does not sell or transfer ownership.

## 8. Third-party components

The Software includes or loads third-party components (for example libmpv and
FFmpeg, Flutter and Dart packages, Rust crates, fonts, and the files under
`rust_builder/cargokit/`). Each of them stays under its own license, which
takes precedence over this Agreement for that component. Their notices are
kept with their source, and the app lists the licenses of the components it
includes (Settings > About > Licenses).

Nothing in this Agreement limits the rights those licenses give you. In
particular:

- where a component is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License
  (such as the libmpv and FFmpeg builds the app loads as shared libraries), you
  may replace or modify that library, and reverse engineer the Software as far
  as needed to debug such modifications;
- the source of components under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 is available
  from their own projects, and that license, not this Agreement, applies to
  those files.

## 9. Plugins

Plugins are not part of the Software. Each plugin, whether installed from a
repository, a file or a link, is provided by its author under its own terms.
The owner does not control third-party plugins or the services they reach, and
is not responsible for them. You are responsible for using plugins, and the
content they reach, lawfully.

## 10. Earlier versions

Versions of this repository published before the effective date were released
under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later. Copies of those
versions stay under that license. This Agreement applies to every version from
the effective date onward.

## 11. Paid features and accounts

Kanaru may offer optional paid features. They are provided separately, may need
an account and may have their own terms. Paying for them does not change the
rights in this Agreement for the rest of the Software.

## 12. Contributions

Contributions are welcome. By submitting a contribution you agree that it may
be included in the Software under this Agreement. Contributions from people
outside the project need a signed Contributor License Agreement before they
are merged (see `CONTRIBUTING.md`).

## 13. Data and privacy

- The Software collects no analytics, crash reports or usage tracking, and it
  does not send your music or library data anywhere by itself.
- Network access happens only for features you use. Plugins you install send
  data to the hosts they list, which the app shows before you install them.
- If you sign in to an account, the account service stores your email address,
  your devices and your purchases, only to provide the paid features. How that
  data is kept, for how long and how to delete it is set out in the privacy
  policy (`PRIVACY.md`) published before the account service opens.
- Logs are stored on your device and leave it only if you share them yourself.

## 14. No warranty

To the extent allowed by law, the Software is provided "as is", without
warranty of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness
for a particular purpose and non-infringement.

## 15. Limitation of liability

To the extent allowed by law, the owner is not liable for any damages arising
from the use of, or the inability to use, the Software. Nothing in this
Agreement limits rights that consumer law gives you and that cannot be waived.

## 16. Termination

This license ends only if you break this Agreement. If you stop the breach
within 30 days after the owner tells you about it, your license is restored,
unless you have broken this Agreement before. When the license ends, you must
stop using the Software and delete your copies.

## 17. Governing law

This Agreement is governed by the laws of Vietnam, and disputes go to the
competent courts of Vietnam. This does not take away protections that the
consumer law of the country where you live gives you and that cannot be waived.

## 18. Severability and entire agreement

If a court finds part of this Agreement unenforceable, that part is applied as
far as the law allows and the rest stays in force. This Agreement, together
with the licenses of third-party components (section 8) and any separate terms
for paid features (section 11), is the whole agreement between you and the
owner about the Software.

## 19. Changes

The owner may change this Agreement for later versions of the Software. The
version shipped with a release applies to that release.

## 20. Contact

Requests for written permission and questions about this Agreement go to the
contact address above.
